KNOWNBUG: minimal header-free form of cpp17_tuple_basic's remaining blocker
(std::make_tuple at arity >= 3).  A constructor template constrained by a
SFINAE default argument whose constexpr callee is a member of another class
template and uses its OWN parameter pack (sizeof...(Us)) is not a viable
candidate when the construction happens inside a function template's
instantiated body: overload resolution fails ("found no match"), the failure
is swallowed, and the calling function template gets no body (nondet return).
Every ingredient verified necessary by single-dimension toggling; g++ and
clang++ accept and run this (assert holds at runtime).  Flip to CORE when the
constrained constructor resolves.
